 "name": "primes-10",
 "origin": "programs/primes.imp",
 "provenance": "krun (K 7.1.337 frontend) on the kdist kimp LLVM definition (kompiled by K v7.1.318, imp-semantics 683a773)",
 "source": "// Port of k-distribution/tests/regression-new/imp-llvm/primes.imp (K tutorial IMP) to kimp IMP.\n// It counts in s all the prime numbers up to m.\n// kimp has no declarations, so `int i, m, n, q, r, s, t, x, y, z;` becomes explicit zero initialisation.\n// The parameter N is the literal of the line that starts with `m =` (s = 4 when N is 10).\n\ni = 0;\nq = 0;\nr = 0;\ns = 0;\nt = 0;\nx = 0;\ny = 0;\nz = 0;\nm = 10;  n = 2;\nwhile (n <= m) {\n  // checking primality of n and writing t to 1 or 0\n  i = 2;  q = n/i;  t = 1;\n  while (i<=q && 1<=t) {\n    x = i;\n    y = q;\n    // fast multiplication (base 2) algorithm\n    z = 0;\n    while (!(x <= 0)) {\n      q = x/2;\n      r = q+q + 1;\n      if (r <= x) { z = z+y; } else {}\n      x = q;\n      y = y+y;\n    } // end fast multiplication\n    if (n <= z) { t = 0; } else { i = i + 1;  q = n/i; }\n  } // end checking primality\n  if (1 <= t) { s = s + 1; } else {}\n  n = n + 1;\n}\n"
}
